From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:51:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give a game behind Cartouche's console its own scene on a TV

iOS 27 hands an app a TV, by cable or AirPlay, as a scene of its own
only for a scene accessory that the app registers; otherwise it mirrors
the iPhone. A game that runs in LiveProcess registers its accessory in
its own process, whose scenes Cartouche hosts: iOS never hears of it,
and the TV would show the iPhone's screen, the game's controls
included. Cartouche registers one itself while a game runs behind its
console (launcher/Sources/CartoucheTV.swift).

The app delegate gives the TV's scene Cartouche's TV scene delegate, in
case iOS asks it for that role's configuration, never LiveContainer's
own scene delegate.

AppSceneViewController opens a second scene of the game's process on
the TV's screen, with the specification of the scene SpringBoard gave
an app for an external screen before iOS 27: the game's UIKit asks its
delegate for that role's configuration, and nxnative answers with its
TV scene, where it moves its picture and plays docked while the iPhone
keeps the controls. The scene follows the game's own into the
background and closes with the game's process.

