+// Cartouche: a second scene of the app's process, on an external display
+// such as a TV, as iOS would give the app one for it before iOS 27: the app
+// fills it itself (nxnative moves its picture there, DmTVSceneDelegate).
+// Nil when this iOS has no such scene, or when the app does not run. The
+// view controller shows the scene: its owner puts it in the display's
+// window, and takes it out again before closing the scene.
+- (UIViewController *)openExternalDisplaySceneOnScreen:(UIScreen *)screen API_AVAILABLE(ios(18.0)) NS_SWIFT_NAME(openExternalDisplayScene(on:));
